ng impurities or varying the  sulfur content but more times than not  it's cheaper to use these oils in their  natural state than try to convert them  into a different state light crude oil  is generally the most valuable type of  oil given that it's the easiest to  refine it and has the largest amount of  use cases this is the type of oil that  is used to produce gasoline Diesel and  aviation fuel in other words this is the  type of oil that runs the world heavy  crude oil on the other hand it is also  pretty useful given that it's what's  used in most manufacturing processes and  crude plays an essential role in  producing Industrial Products such as  asphalt and Plastics with the light and  heavier out of the way that leaves us  with medium crude oil which is usually  the most underappreciated medium crude  is actually the most common type of oil  but there aren't very many use cases for  it in its natural state so medium crude  is usually distilled to create light  crude in terms of the subcategories  sweet food is what the world craves in  and sour crude is generally just  converted it into sweet crew with that  being said the most valuable type of oil  has historically been a light sweet  crude due to the exponential growth  within the automotive and Aviation  Industries but as the world's oil  consumption started to stabilize it  became evident that oil Giants may have  diverted too much of their focus to  light sweet crude we were starting to  get into a position where there was an  oversupply of light crude and then under  supplier of heavy crude so while light  speed has historically demanded a  premium much of that premium has slowly  eroded away over the years and in some  cases I could even trade at a discount I  know that all of that info may have been  a little dense but I think it's  important in understanding a country's  complex oil needs now that we have a  basic technical understanding regarding  the various types of oil let's delve  into why Sau